        "rationale": "The structural obligations in `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.agent_config.settings` are all covered by the supplied roots. The rest is observable behavior or is delegated to refining requirements.\n\nCovered structural obligations:\n- **Variants and tag.** The text says \"Each `AgentConfig` variant carries the corresponding settings\" and that serde uses the `backend` field to select `bedrock`, `openai` or `ollama`. A flat struct, or a tag under a different name, would break this. `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/config.rs#enum[AgentConfig]` declares `Bedrock(BedrockConfig)`, `OpenAi(OpenAiConfig)` and `Ollama(OllamaConfig)`. It uses `#[serde(tag = \"backend\", rename_all = \"lowercase\")]` with `openai` renamed.\n- **`OptionValue` variants.** The text says it is \"a `String`, `Boolean`, `Integer(i64)`, `Float(f64)`, `Array`, or `Map`\", with arrays holding option values and maps associating strings with option values. These serialize as the corresponding untagged values. `#[serde(untagged)] enum[OptionValue]` has exactly these variants, with `Vec<OptionValue>` and `BTreeMap<String, OptionValue>` for the nested cases.\n- **`BedrockCredentials` fields.** The text says it \"contains `access_key_id` and `secret_access_key`, both `SecretString`, and an optional `session_token` of the same type\". `struct[BedrockCredentials]` has those three fields with those types.\n- **`SecretString` interface.** The text says to \"Construct a `SecretString` from `String` or `&str`\" and that `expose_secret()` borrows its value. It also says serialization preserves the string. `struct[SecretString]` is a `#[serde(transparent)]` newtype. `impl[SecretString/From<String>]` and `impl[SecretString/From<&str>]` provide the two constructors. `impl[SecretString]/fn[expose_secret]` returns `&str`.\n\nNot structural, or covered elsewhere:\n- **Debug output.** `Debug` printing `<redacted>` is observable behavior. The implementation, `impl[SecretString/fmt::Debug]/fn[fmt]`, is also owned by the refining `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.SecretString`.\n- **Defaults and empty `options`.** The OpenAI defaults, the Ollama default and the empty `options` map at construction are observable results. Any construction that yields them satisfies the text.\n- **`option(key, value)` replacement.** The insert-or-replace semantics are likewise observable. The `option` methods and the `options` field types belong to the refining `BedrockConfig`, `OpenAiConfig` and `OllamaConfig` requirements. The settings text only says to choose those config types.\n- **Nonfinite-float rejection.** This is behavior, implemented by `impl[OptionValue]/fn[validate]`. The text prescribes no particular algorithm.\n\nNo further implementation roots are needed."
