        "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover each behavioral obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.agent_config.settings`. They are all in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/config.rs` under `mod[tests]`.\n\n- **Backend selection and settings in the same object:** `fn[all_backends_preserve_nested_settings_and_credentials]` round-trips bedrock, openai and ollama JSON objects with a `backend` tag. It asserts the serialized value and the deserialized copy are equal. `fn[openai_inference_options_only_fill_missing_defaults]` deserializes `{\"backend\":\"openai\"}` and checks it equals `AgentConfig::OpenAi(OpenAiConfig::new())`.\n- **Defaults:** `fn[option_defaults_and_credential_resolution_are_deterministic]` asserts the OpenAI model `gpt-6.1-sol` and endpoint `https://api.openai.com/v1`. It also asserts the Ollama endpoint `http://localhost:11434`. `fn[openai_uses_the_default_credential_variable]` runs a child process with `OPENAI_API_KEY` set and asserts `OpenAiConfig::new().resolved_api_key()` returns that value. That is the correct way to test it, because it needs process environment state.\n- **Empty options at construction:** `fn[backend_builders_set_only_the_requested_fields]` serializes freshly built configs. The output has no `options` key, so the options map starts empty.\n- **`option(key, value)`:** the same test chains `a=1`, `b=true`, then `a=2` on all three backends. It asserts the result is `{\"a\":2,\"b\":true}`, so a repeated key is replaced and the other key is preserved.\n- **`OptionValue` variants and untagged serialization:** the nested test round-trips a String, Integer, Float, Boolean, Array and Map. `fn[option_defaults_and_credential_resolution_are_deterministic]` checks that `1` deserializes to `Integer` and `1.0` to `Float`.\n- **Nonfinite floats rejected:** `options_json` on an Ollama config with a NaN nested in an array returns an error. `OptionValue::validate` on a map containing a nested infinity returns an error. The shared `AgentConfig::options_json` loops over every backend's options and calls `validate`. That is the check the backend calls rely on.\n- **`BedrockCredentials`:** `fn[backend_builders_set_only_the_requested_fields]` checks serialization and deserialization with and without the optional `session_token`.\n- **`SecretString`:** `fn[configuration_debug_hides_credentials]` checks construction from `&str` and from `String`, `expose_secret()`, `Debug` printing `<redacted>`, and serialization preserving the string.\n\nI found no obligation that is untested or asserted wrongly, and I found no missing markers."
